WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.892
"The death toll continues to rise

00:00:05.892 --> 00:00:08.353
at a fatal gas line explosion in Mexico."

00:00:08.353 --> 00:00:09.980
"Authorities say that the pipeline

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.983
had been ruptured by
suspected oil thieves."

00:00:12.983 --> 00:00:14.568
People were lighting cigarettes,

00:00:14.568 --> 00:00:15.402
they were dancing,

00:00:15.402 --> 00:00:17.988
they were throwing gasoline
on top of each other.

00:00:17.988 --> 00:00:19.906
Completely intoxicated by the fumes.

00:00:19.906 --> 00:00:21.033
"They took their fill

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:23.535
as soldiers sent to guard
the pipeline looked on

00:00:23.535 --> 00:00:25.245
seemingly powerless.

00:00:25.245 --> 00:00:26.204
Then this happened."

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.587
And essentially in a matter of seconds,

00:00:33.587 --> 00:00:35.631
the whole thing ignited.

00:00:36.965 --> 00:00:39.051
People were running from the blast

00:00:39.051 --> 00:00:40.594
like human torches.

00:00:41.136 --> 00:00:43.930
It was complete chaos.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.308
"The most important thing now

00:00:46.308 --> 00:00:47.643
is to look after the injured,

00:00:47.643 --> 00:00:48.518
to save lives.

00:00:48.518 --> 00:00:50.228
That is the most important thing.

00:00:50.228 --> 00:00:52.147
The fight against the
illegal theft of fuel

00:00:52.147 --> 00:00:53.774
will be strengthened."

00:00:53.774 --> 00:00:55.609
The state loses in the region of

00:00:55.609 --> 00:00:57.486
three billion U.S. dollars a year

00:00:57.486 --> 00:01:01.448
and the 95 percent of what is known as

00:01:01.448 --> 00:01:02.449
tomas clandestinas,

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:04.326
which are illegal extractions,

00:01:04.326 --> 00:01:07.245
are done by big cartels.

00:01:15.671 --> 00:01:16.922
My name is Matthew Bremner

00:01:16.922 --> 00:01:18.590
I'm a Scottish writer.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:22.552
I wrote the story about Mexico's
biggest pipeline explosion.

00:01:25.013 --> 00:01:27.432
Within the first sort of 24 hours,

00:01:27.432 --> 00:01:29.101
people said there were 20 people dead

00:01:29.101 --> 00:01:30.894
and 71 people injured.

00:01:30.894 --> 00:01:33.271
Obviously those numbers rocketed up

00:01:33.271 --> 00:01:36.108
but the final death
toll, as it were, is 134.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:43.073
Now in the field where
the irrigation trench was

00:01:43.073 --> 00:01:44.908
where the pipeline runs,

00:01:44.908 --> 00:01:48.704
framed by an old tree which
was scorched in the blast

00:01:48.704 --> 00:01:50.372
there is now a shrine.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:55.460
Almost every day, relatives
of the victims go there.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:59.381
They sit on little plastic
benches or wooden crates.

00:01:59.381 --> 00:02:03.552
They stare at the crosses, often crying.

00:02:03.552 --> 00:02:06.054
Sometimes in some sort of trance.

00:02:06.054 --> 00:02:07.597
And they spend hours there.

00:02:08.682 --> 00:02:11.226
It's the same always in society,

00:02:11.226 --> 00:02:12.978
the people who are at
the bottom of the tree,

00:02:12.978 --> 00:02:14.730
the people that were there

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.107
looking to take advantage
of an opportunity.

00:02:17.107 --> 00:02:18.900
They're the people that always suffer.

00:02:24.656 --> 00:02:27.576
The scale of oil theft
in Mexico is enormous.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.371
The state loses 3 billion
US dollars a year.

00:02:32.205 --> 00:02:34.666
Huachicolero, which is
the illegal siphoning

00:02:34.666 --> 00:02:37.210
and tapping of fuel

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:38.295
which has been happening in Mexico

00:02:38.295 --> 00:02:41.256
now for about 25 years, perhaps longer.

00:02:41.256 --> 00:02:44.009
What was a very informal industry

00:02:44.009 --> 00:02:46.678
has now become something
which is far more organized.

00:02:46.678 --> 00:02:48.138
A lot of the big Mexican cartels

00:02:48.138 --> 00:02:51.141
are now branching into
this sale of oil theft.

00:02:51.975 --> 00:02:55.270
Half of their business is now focused

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:57.147
on illegal fuel tapping.

00:02:58.482 --> 00:03:01.568
It's a lot less risky, essentially,

00:03:01.568 --> 00:03:03.612
to get involved in illegal fuel trade

00:03:03.612 --> 00:03:06.490
because you don't need to
transport drugs across borders.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:07.532
You don't need to pay off

00:03:07.532 --> 00:03:09.951
different types of police
in different countries.

00:03:11.536 --> 00:03:14.956
The corruption inside
the big petrol giant,

00:03:14.956 --> 00:03:18.960
in this case Petróleos
Mexicanos, Pemex, is rampant.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.047
And so it's quite easy to
pay off workers inside,

00:03:22.047 --> 00:03:23.715
to find out when the oil is flowing

00:03:23.715 --> 00:03:25.175
through certain pipelines

00:03:25.175 --> 00:03:26.718
and to rob it

00:03:26.718 --> 00:03:29.221
and then sell it domestically
on the black market.

00:03:34.059 --> 00:03:36.561
Pemex is one of the biggest
oil companies in the world.

00:03:36.561 --> 00:03:40.357
For a long time it was
considered a cash cow

00:03:40.357 --> 00:03:42.526
for the Mexican economy.

00:03:42.526 --> 00:03:45.111
It kept Mexico afloat in many ways

00:03:45.111 --> 00:03:46.363
and people always refer to it

00:03:46.363 --> 00:03:51.076
as the most important
institution that the country had.

00:03:54.079 --> 00:03:56.289
The government recently released figures

00:03:56.289 --> 00:04:01.044
that around 80 percent
of the tomas clandestinas

00:04:01.044 --> 00:04:03.547
and the fuel robberies
that take place in Mexico

00:04:03.547 --> 00:04:06.967
are organized in some
way by insiders in Pemex.

00:04:08.385 --> 00:04:10.053
What would normally happen

00:04:10.053 --> 00:04:13.390
is that they would have
a link inside Pemex

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.852
who would tell them through
which pipeline a certain,

00:04:16.852 --> 00:04:18.687
it could be gasoline, it could be gas,

00:04:18.687 --> 00:04:19.729
it could be anything,

00:04:19.729 --> 00:04:22.524
is running and what
time and what the pressure is.

00:04:22.524 --> 00:04:26.194
They would then go down
to the specific pipeline

00:04:26.194 --> 00:04:27.237
normally at nighttime.

00:04:27.237 --> 00:04:29.447
Normally the pipes are about

00:04:29.447 --> 00:04:32.909
between one or two
meters below the ground.

00:04:32.909 --> 00:04:35.120
They would dig to get to the pipeline.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.248
Then would perforate it
with a high-powered drill.

00:04:38.248 --> 00:04:40.834
Then a professional solderer would come in

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.461
and he would solder a tap to the pipe.

00:04:46.131 --> 00:04:47.257
They know exactly what they're doing

00:04:47.257 --> 00:04:48.341
when they do it

00:04:48.341 --> 00:04:51.803
and the risks that it entails.

00:04:51.803 --> 00:04:53.054
So they're professionals.

00:04:55.515 --> 00:04:58.768
One of the huachicoleros in Hidalgo area

00:04:58.768 --> 00:05:00.562
told me that in one night

00:05:00.562 --> 00:05:02.105
the organization that he works for

00:05:02.105 --> 00:05:04.065
can make up to 90 thousand pesos.

00:05:04.065 --> 00:05:05.150
If you take into account

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.736
that an average wage,

00:05:07.736 --> 00:05:09.446
at least in that area from
what people were telling me,

00:05:09.446 --> 00:05:11.615
is about 15 hundred pesos a week.

00:05:11.615 --> 00:05:14.284
Then, you know, we're
talking serious money here.

00:05:21.666 --> 00:05:23.793
Around midday there was
a rumor that was spread

00:05:23.793 --> 00:05:25.921
that a pipeline had been perforated

00:05:25.921 --> 00:05:29.132
and that people were
illegally siphoning gasoline

00:05:29.132 --> 00:05:31.968
from one of the biggest
pipelines in Mexico.

00:05:34.346 --> 00:05:36.431
Around two thirty in the afternoon

00:05:36.431 --> 00:05:40.977
a patrol of 25 officers
from the military arrived.

00:05:42.729 --> 00:05:45.649
So this was quite an unusual occurrence

00:05:45.649 --> 00:05:48.318
simply because normally fuel robberies

00:05:48.318 --> 00:05:49.653
would take place at night.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.989
Men, women, and children were turning up

00:05:52.989 --> 00:05:57.994
in vans, in cars, on foot,
and on bicycles and motorbikes

00:05:58.411 --> 00:06:00.372
and coming to the area in huge numbers.

00:06:03.291 --> 00:06:05.335
Within the next two-to-three hours

00:06:05.335 --> 00:06:07.295
what may have been 80 people

00:06:07.295 --> 00:06:08.922
soon was six times that.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.549
It felt like they were almost celebrating

00:06:11.549 --> 00:06:12.425
in some sort of way.

00:06:12.425 --> 00:06:14.844
It felt like a water
party, I heard people say.

00:06:14.844 --> 00:06:17.389
Generally, they were
just local townspeople

00:06:17.389 --> 00:06:21.935
who were taking advantage of
the situation to get free fuel.

00:06:24.062 --> 00:06:25.605
One thing that's very important here

00:06:25.605 --> 00:06:27.232
is the fuel that was running

00:06:27.232 --> 00:06:30.527
through this particular
pipeline was very high octane.

00:06:30.527 --> 00:06:31.778
Which meant that it released

00:06:31.778 --> 00:06:34.155
lots of very, very, flammable gasses.

00:06:34.155 --> 00:06:36.574
Because the day itself was relatively hot,

00:06:36.574 --> 00:06:40.996
these gasses were sort of
floating above the crowd.

00:06:40.996 --> 00:06:43.123
It hadn't yet got to the stage

00:06:43.123 --> 00:06:45.250
where it was low enough to be ignited.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:49.546
So around six o'clock when
it began to get darker

00:06:49.546 --> 00:06:50.797
and the temperature dropped,

00:06:50.797 --> 00:06:52.507
those gasses also dropped.

00:06:52.507 --> 00:06:54.884
And so they sort of began
to smother the crowd.

00:06:57.303 --> 00:06:59.639
Now the interesting thing is that the fire

00:06:59.639 --> 00:07:01.683
created inside a cigarette butt

00:07:01.683 --> 00:07:04.477
is not hot enough to ignite petrol

00:07:04.477 --> 00:07:07.188
but what is hot enough
is static electricity.

00:07:07.188 --> 00:07:09.149
And what would have probably happened

00:07:09.149 --> 00:07:11.151
is that a static shock would
have come from somewhere

00:07:11.151 --> 00:07:13.194
where there were two hands
that were being shaken

00:07:13.194 --> 00:07:14.821
or friction created between two people

00:07:14.821 --> 00:07:16.114
rubbing up against each other.

00:07:16.114 --> 00:07:17.824
And that would have created a static shock

00:07:17.824 --> 00:07:19.159
which would have been hot enough

00:07:19.159 --> 00:07:20.201
to ignite these gasses

00:07:20.201 --> 00:07:21.703
which had now sunk down.

00:07:21.703 --> 00:07:23.663
And essentially within
a matter of seconds,

00:07:23.663 --> 00:07:25.540
the whole thing ignited.

00:07:31.463 --> 00:07:36.468
And as the ignition of the fire settles down somewhat

00:07:36.468 --> 00:07:38.803
then you see the people
running from the blast.

00:07:38.803 --> 00:07:41.222
And this is perhaps the
most impactful moment

00:07:41.222 --> 00:07:43.016
because the people that
are running from the blast

00:07:43.016 --> 00:07:44.225
are in flames.

00:07:44.225 --> 00:07:45.185
Some of them trip over.

00:07:45.185 --> 00:07:47.145
Some of them run towards the road.

00:07:47.145 --> 00:07:48.646
Some of them are rolling on the ground.

00:07:48.646 --> 00:07:50.857
Some of them are crying for water.

00:07:54.027 --> 00:07:55.862
The local paramedics came in first

00:07:55.862 --> 00:07:56.946
from the surrounding villages

00:07:56.946 --> 00:07:58.448
and when they got to the field,

00:07:58.448 --> 00:08:03.119
they saw people sort of
writhing on the floor in agony.

00:08:03.119 --> 00:08:08.124
They saw charred bodies that
were completely incinerated.

00:08:08.333 --> 00:08:10.126
Sort of falling apart.

00:08:10.126 --> 00:08:12.921
People that were in their
last moments of agony but 

00:08:12.921 --> 00:08:14.964
burned into that position.

00:08:14.964 --> 00:08:16.883
What they saw was the most horrific thing

00:08:16.883 --> 00:08:19.052
that you could possibly
see, I can imagine.

00:08:42.075 --> 00:08:46.371
The Mexican government has
declared war on huachicolero.

00:08:47.664 --> 00:08:48.498
Are they winning it?

00:08:48.498 --> 00:08:50.542
I think it's far too early to say.

00:08:50.542 --> 00:08:51.793
Will they win it?

00:08:51.793 --> 00:08:55.380
Well I think if the drug
war is anything to go by

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.506
then probably not.

